    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of the change implementing the `customerCode` assignment:\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` endpoint is an OfficeFloor function pipeline. I added a new step to it and surfaced the value on the response DTO.\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Database schemas** \u2014 added a `customer_code` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (`hsqldb` \u2014 used by tests, plus `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). Seed inserts use explicit column lists, so existing data is unaffected (existing owners just have a null code).\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` field on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name onto the GET/create responses.\n\n4. **New function** (`AssignCustomerCode.java`) \u2014 computes `sequence = ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` (one more than the current number of owners), takes the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`, and sets `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", last3, sequence)` (e.g. `SMI-0007`). It mutates the `@Val Owner` in place, so `SaveOwner` persists it.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** (`owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 inserted the `assignCustomerCode` step under transaction governance, after `applyRegistrationDate` and before `save`, so the code is computed before the new owner is counted itself and committed with the rest of the request.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` test passes: two consecutive creates produce `SMI-####` and `JON-####` with globally consecutive sequence numbers.",
